  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Design Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s design specifications. My focus is on the requested aesthetics, specifically the clean, mobile-first educational platform design. I\'m noting the preference for a white background with subtle blue accents and soft gray tones, and I\'ve also begun logging the hex codes associated with the requested color palette. I\'m making sure to consider mobile-first design principles.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve been solidifying the visual aesthetics, starting with color schemes such as bg-slate-50, bg-white, and border-slate-200. I\'m focusing on a premium, minimal, and elegant design with rounded corners, clean typography, smooth animations, and professional spacing. I\'m also planning dark mode toggle support. I\'m taking cues from top platforms like Unacademy, Physics Wallah, and others.\n\n**Structuring Navigation & Header**\n\nI\'m now detailing the navigation and header elements. I\'m incorporating the logo (\"Sneha Gupta (CA Finalist)\") with a professional badge. The navigation will include links for Home, Courses, Mentorship, Strategy Sessions, Testimonials, and FAQs. I\'m incorporating auth buttons, a student dashboard link, an admin panel badge, a mobile navigation drawer, and a quick search and filter bar across courses and mentorship sections.\n\n**Designing Home Page Elements**\n\nI\'ve started designing the home page, specifically focusing on the hero section. I\'m integrating the \"Sneha Gupta (CA Finalist)\" branding with a placeholder for a professional portrait. The section will display badges highlighting her qualifications. I\'m also preparing a brief introduction with a motivational headline.\n\n\n**Outlining Home Page Content**\n\nI\'m now detailing the home page content sections, including \"Why Study With Sneha\" with its four key pillars and featured courses displayed as preview cards. I\'m also planning a section showcasing Mentorship Programs and a booking feature for Strategy Sessions. Student testimonials will be presented in a carousel format, and an FAQ section will be provided. The design also incorporates a contact section with an inquiry form. Lastly, I\'m incorporating a footer with quick links and social links.\n\nI\'m also working on detailed specifications for the courses and the corresponding course detail pages. Specifically, I\'m designing chapter-wise course cards, and each will display relevant information such as course details, price, and \"Buy Now\" options. I\'m including filters by CA level and by subject.\n\n\n**Detailing Course & Mentorship Pages**\n\nI\'m now detailing the course and mentorship pages. For courses, I\'m working on the course detail view, including descriptions, chapter breakdowns, video previews, and student reviews. Post-purchase, courses are immediately unlocked in the dashboard. I am also detailing the Mentorship page layout, with options and benefits for CA Inter students.\n\n\n**Formulating Student Interactions**\n\nI\'m now detailing post-payment workflows. I\'ll integrate a student information form to capture vital data for student profiles and admin views, including attempt details and prep level. I\'ve also detailed the Personal Strategy Session page with price, features, and booking details. I\'m finalizing the booking form, incorporating a date picker, time slot selection, contact number, and struggle area, all leading to a Razorpay checkout and instant booking confirmation.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Review System**\n\nI\'m now implementing the admin review system. I\'m focusing on user interface elements. I\'m incorporating features such as WhatsApp feedback screenshot cards and photo badges. I\'m enabling admins to add reviews easily, including student name, exam score, and image uploads. I\'m also implementing the option to add ratings and quotes, simplifying the review creation process.\n\n**Configuring Authentication**\n\nI\'m now configuring login, register, and authentication features. I\'m incorporating email login and register with role selection for students and admins, as well as a \"forgot password\" modal. I\'m also integrating \"Demo Admin Mode\" with pre-configured credentials for testing. I\'m ensuring student account data persistence across sessions.\n\n**Designing Student Dashboard**\n\nI am now designing the student dashboard. I\'m including a tabbed, clean layout displaying purchased products and recommendations. I\'m organizing the dashboard tabs to include My Courses with progress indicators and a resume feature, Continue Learning with direct links to the last watched video, Notes & Question Banks with PDF viewer, and Purchased Mentorship sections.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Student Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating enhanced student features. I\'m prioritizing a weekly timetable view and incorporating mentor chat/WhatsApp buttons and weekly target submission status. For strategy sessions, I\'ll display upcoming call details, Zoom links, and submitted preparation profiles. The profile & settings section will enable name, phone, attempt details, and password changes. I\'m focusing on the video player component with LMS features: responsive design, playback controls, chapter list, progress tracking, and embedded notes/discussion.\n\n\n**Refining Admin & Payment Views**\n\nI\'m currently focused on enhancing the admin and payment sections. I\'m building out the admin views for strategy sessions, testimonials, student lists, and purchase histories, adding filter and editing capabilities. I\'m also simulating the Razorpay payment gateway to enable interactive order processing, and a confetti animation, with instant verification and enrollment unlock. I\'m also implementing a timetable utility for study planning.\n\n\n**Defining Data Architecture**\n\nI\'m now defining the data architecture, focusing on `/src/data/initialData.ts` which will include rich sample data. I\'m also planning the `AuthContext.tsx` and `DataContext.tsx` for state management. Further, I\'m working on the `Navbar.tsx`, `Footer.tsx` and `Hero.tsx` components to define core interface elements. I\'m building a robust and realistic sample data set.\n\n\n**Organizing Homepage Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the home page components, including the \"Why Study With Sneha\" section with its core pillars and stats. I\'m also adding a carousel of featured courses, mentorship summary cards, and a highlight card for 1:1 strategy sessions. Student reviews with marksheets and WhatsApp feedback are being incorporated, alongside an FAQ accordion and contact form, and I\'m also preparing reusable course cards and the course detail view. Further, I\'m working on the mentorship option card and its corresponding post-payment form.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 575412489
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
